{"type":"message","id":"08a7874b","parentId":"dbd3651f","timestamp":"2026-05-26T00:14:12.146Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants to know how I would add a manual pause/resume feature with a one-line command. Let me think about the cleanest approach.\n\nCurrently the circuit breaker has `paused_until` field that's checked before trading. The simplest approach would be to:\n\n1. Add a flag file (like `/tmp/crypto_trading_paused` or `~/.openclaw/workspace/crypto/trading_paused`) \n2. The monitor checks this file before every trade signal\n3. `touch /tmp/crypto_trading_paused` to pause, `rm /tmp/crypto_trading_paused` to resume\n\nOr even simpler - use the circuit breaker's pause mechanism but expose a manual trigger in manual_trade.py. Like adding a `pause` and `resume` command that sets `circuit_breaker.paused_until` to a far future date.\n\nBut actually the simplest approach for the monitor would be to check a lock file on disk - that way it survives restarts and can be toggled from command line with `touch`/`rm`.\n\nLet me just explain the approach without actually implementing it.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"思路很简单——用文件锁：\n\n**暂停**：在 `~/.openclaw/workspace/crypto/` 下 touch 一个空文件，比如 `trading_paused`\n**恢复**：删掉这个文件\n\nmonitor 每次要下单前先检查这个文件存不存在，存在就跳过并记录「手动暂停中」。一行命令就是：\n\n```bash\ntouch 那个文件  # 暂停\nrm 那个文件     # 恢复\n```\n\n比改代码重启优雅，也不影响配置。"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":303,"output":582,"cacheRead":32000,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":32885,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779754443693}}
