{"type":"message","id":"ce954292","parentId":"9bfa0a70","timestamp":"2026-05-26T07:31:04.685Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking if changing STOP_LOSS_PCT to 2% will affect all order types, including stop loss orders. They're worried that the stop loss orders might still use 1%.\n\nLet me trace through the code flow again:\n\n1. The central function `calc_tp_sl()` in crypto_signal_monitor.py uses `STOP_LOSS_PCT` to compute `sl_price`\n2. Every place that creates orders calls `calc_tp_sl()` to get the SL price\n3. The SL price is then passed to `binance_auto_trade.py` which submits the order to Binance\n\nSo yes, changing the single `STOP_LOSS_PCT = 0.01` to `0.02` will make ALL future orders use 2% stop loss. There's no separate \"delegation order\" that uses a different SL calculation - everything flows through the same function.\n\nThe user is asking this question because they may have been confused by my previous answer. Let me be very clear: changing this one variable changes the SL for EVERYTHING - market orders, signal orders, manual orders, everything. All new positions will have 2% SL.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"不会。`calc_tp_sl()` 是整个系统唯一计算止损价的地方，开仓信号、手动开仓、恢复持仓全走它。改 `STOP_LOSS_PCT = 0.02` 之后，新开的每一单——无论市价单还是委托止损单——拿到的都是 2% 算出来的价格，不存在某个角落偷偷还用 1% 的情况。\n\n只有一个例外：已经挂着的老单（比如现在 BNB 那个空单的止损单），它的 SL 价格是开仓时算好提交给币安的，改代码不影响它。新开的单子全部 2%。"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":651,"output":628,"cacheRead":65280,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":66559,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779780653834}}
