{"type":"message","id":"9f153fca","parentId":"35e54f84","timestamp":"2026-05-26T07:34:30.856Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The manual_trade.py relies on crypto_state.json for prices. ETC is not in our monitored coins. Let me try a different approach - get the ETC price from Binance testnet directly and open manually using binance_auto_trade.py.\n\nOr actually, let me just add ETC price to the state file temporarily. Actually, that's hacky. Let me just get the price from the testnet API and use the binance_auto_trade module directly.\n\nActually wait - let me try a simpler approach. Let me just fetch the ETC price from testnet API and then call manual_trade with it. But manual_trade doesn't support a manual price parameter... \n\nLet me check if I can write a small script that uses binance_auto_trade to open the position directly.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_SPrX4kBQwZRoUKNEgyGL6760","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace && python3 -c \"\nimport sys, json\nsys.path.insert(0, 'scripts')\nfrom binance_auto_trade import request, get_quantity_precision, format_price\n\n# 拿 ETC 价格\nticker = request('GET', '/fapi/v1/ticker/price', {'symbol': 'ETCUSDT'})\nprint(f'ETC 当前价:', ticker)\n\nif isinstance(ticker, dict) and 'price' in ticker:\n    price = float(ticker['price'])\n    print(f'ETC 价格: \\${price}')\nelse:\n    print('获取价格失败:', ticker)\n\" 2>&1 | grep -v 'InsecureRequest\\|warnings.warn\\|urllib3\\|INFO'","timeout":15}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":124,"output":560,"cacheRead":69504,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":70188,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779780862972}}
